From e45a33863de4392826069de8cde503f2473cf802 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:22:23 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18b: expose find in page over FindTabHelper

Route WebContentsDelegate::FindReply to Chromium's FindTabHelper, as Browser does, and add a thin per-tab adapter that observes its results. ReArcTabFindStart always opens a new numbered session (match-case and forward options), ReArcTabFindNext moves forward or backward with wrap, and ReArcTabFindStop clears, keeps or activates the selection. Result events carry match count, active ordinal and the final flag. Every session ends with exactly one terminal event: navigated on a primary cross-document commit, closed before tab.closed, stopped, or replaced.

Advertise find_in_page in ABI 1.16 / bridge 0.18.0 with additive symbols only and unchanged ABI 1.13/1.14 layouts. Build p52; the new native find host checks counts, ordinals, case, direction, invalid arguments and each terminal reason. All native hosts, G1-G5 and four stress processes / sixteen shutdown tabs pass in gates-tab034.log (a first run hit a load-induced evaluation timeout in the profiles host, kept as gates-tab034-fail1.log; the host passed on isolated reruns and the full rerun).

Last rebased: 2026-11-03 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
